  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 142 AM CDT Thu Jul 16 2026\n\nThe mid-level low is expected to begin shifting to the west with the \na ridge building from the east over the next couple days. In the \nmeantime, some residual moisture will combine with the seabreeze to \npromote very low rain chances through at least Friday. For the most \npart though, we will enter a drier period as PWATs come back down to \nclimatological norms for this time of year by this weekend. We can \nexpect heat to be the main story of the forecast per usual. Highs \nwill be back into the lower 105s out west by early next week. Heat \nindices will likely return to the 105-110 range as we head into next \nweek leading to moderate to major heat risk conditions.",
